    "result_text": "There's only one test class, and it passes. The full `./mvnw -o test` build succeeded.\n\nThe implementation is complete and the test suite is green. Here's what I changed to satisfy the salutation specification:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `title` input field to the `OwnerFields` schema, and a read-only `salutation` field to the `Owner` response schema (the DTOs are generated from this spec at build time).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** (model) \u2014 Added a persisted `title` column with getter/setter, so the title survives the `POST` and is available when the owner is read back via `GET`.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `salutation(owner)` derivation and wired it into `toOwnerDto` via a `@Mapping` expression. It returns `title + \" \" + lastName` when a title is present, otherwise just `lastName`. MapStruct maps `title` automatically by name on both input and output.\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 Added the `title` column to the `owners` table. Tests run under the `hsqldb` profile.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreComposesSalutation` (posts `title=DR`, `lastName=who`, expects `salutation` = `\"DR who\"`) passes, and `BUILD SUCCESS` with `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
